sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant H as Handler
    participant S as Store
    participant R as Redis
    C->>H: GET /chat?offset=-1
    H->>H: authorize path · parse offset, cursor, conditional headers, and framing
    H->>S: handleRead → ReadPage(path, offset)
    S->>R: EVALSHA read.lua · HGETALL :meta once
    Note over S,R: capture tail · validate · classify empty / inherited / root-owned
    opt first root snapshot has sliding TTL
        S->>R: HSET accessedAtNs · refresh exact key TTL
    end
    alt root-owned range
        S->>R: same EVALSHA · bounded ZRANGEBYLEX on root :msg
    else inherited fork prefix
        S->>R: later source-slot EVALSHA calls in chronological order
    else empty, at-tail, or beyond-tail range
        Note over S,R: skip every message ZSET
    end
    R-->>S: frame-aligned page + typed fixed snapshot
    S-->>H: messages · next offset · fixed tail
    H->>H: set status, type, ETag, cache, cursor, closure, and next-offset headers
    H-->>C: write complete JSON or binary frames and flush
    loop until the captured tail
        H->>S: ReadPage with same snapshot · no touch
        S->>R: one EVALSHA · validate fixed tail + bounded root range
        S-->>H: messages · next offset · same snapshot
        H-->>C: write page and flush
    end
    H-->>C: finish the body at the fixed tail
    Note over H,R: root-owned page = 1 EVALSHA · 1 metadata HGETALL · no :prod
    Note over H,S: persistent and absolute-expiry-only reads write nothing
    Note over H,S: exceptions: legacy incarnation migration and lazy expiry cleanup
